<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Novgorod First Chronicle</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">13th–15th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Novgorod First Chronicle is the oldest surviving Russian chronicle, compiled in Novgorod and preserved in an older recension, the Synodal <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manuscript">manuscript</a> of the thirteenth and fourteenth centuries, and a younger fifteenth-century recension. Written in a terse local style, it records the city's politics, wars, fires and famines and preserves material on early Rus' that differs from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/primary-chronicle">Primary Chronicle</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/novgorod-first-chronicle.jpg" alt="Novgorod First Chronicle" width="320" height="407" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Nikolay Omonov · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Novgorod_First_Chronicle,_Synod_manuscript_01.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
